/target
/ghidra_proj
/build
*.log
__pycache__/
/.venv
/mutants.out*
/mutants

# The mage's paid save (1000:764e/1000:765d) writes these into the process's
# current directory, so an interactive `cargo run` from the repo root leaves
# them behind -- and a stray save_r?.sav changes the NEXT run's startup path,
# because the slot menu scans the working directory. The five shipped saves
# live in orig/ under their DOS uppercase names and are not matched here.
/save_r?.sav
/places.sav

# Agent tool state, per-machine. The tessl manifest, AGENTS.md and the vendored
# .tessl/ tree ARE tracked -- CLAUDE.md's `@AGENTS.md` include chains through
# them, so a clone that lacked them would silently load nothing.
#
# .claude/ is *mostly* per-machine, but CLAUDE.md's `# Tools` section MUST-uses
# the context-explorer agent and context-search skill as the first
# code-discovery step -- those have to be tracked or a fresh clone has an
# instruction file in force that points at nothing. settings.json registers
# the jbcontext index hooks that section depends on, so it is tracked too.
# Only settings.local.json (machine-local permissions) stays ignored.
# Un-ignoring a path under an ignored directory requires re-including every
# ancestor directory explicitly -- a bare `!` on the leaf is silently a no-op.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/agents/
!/.claude/skills/
!/.claude/settings.json
/.agents/
/.mcp.json
